divergence: prints the flat-kernel token; the Go backend has no flat Jwt.encodeHs256 kernel, so this exact program does not compile on the Go reference. The emitted token is byte-identical to the genuine Go token captured from the equivalent builder-API program Jwt.encode (Jwt.hs256 secret) (claims). The byte equality is asserted in crates/ipec/tests/golden_m5b_uuid_jwt.rs and the runtime jwt unit tests. Ipe records its own output. Divergence from Ipe, rationale: JWT API-surface interim (docs/architecture/divergence-policy.md).
